WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.666 --> 00:00:02.040
SIRI CHERUKURI:
Winter is coming.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.900
Which means we must
always be one and have

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.220
constant vigilance.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.890
STEPHANIE WONG: Yes, we need
to build our walls to keep DDoS

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.480
attacks and data hackers out.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.950
So how do I keep my dragons--

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.930
or better yet, people--
in check from releasing

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.280
confidential data?

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.660
SIRI CHERUKURI: Mobile
Dragon Management, duh.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.544
Or in Google's terms, Mobile
Device Management for G Suite.

00:00:19.544 --> 00:00:21.460
STEPHANIE WONG: I think
we need to see a demo.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.376
SIRI CHERUKURI: All
right, let's jump into it.

00:00:23.376 --> 00:00:26.660
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:33.870
So this is how the G Suite
Admin Console looks like.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.720
First, you need to set up
the Apple Push Notification

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.630
Certificate in the console
to establish a connection

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.670
to the Apple Push
Notification Service,

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.420
which is popularly
called the APNS service,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.920
so that G Suite MDM--

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.940
or any other MDM,
for that matter--

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.290
can efficiently send commands
to all your managed iOS device

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.070
feed.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:56.190
To set it up, you download a
certificate signing request

00:00:56.190 --> 00:01:01.060
from the console, upload it
into the Apple Push Certificate

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.560
Portal by logging in
with your Apple ID.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.600
You will then receive a
signed certificate from Apple.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.240
Download that signed
certificate, and upload it

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.060
back in the G Suite
Admin Console here.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.620
You are now ready to roll.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.320
You can enable MDM
in the setup, and can

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.110
choose if each device
that is being enrolled

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.650
needs to be approved by an admin
before it gets the settings.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:28.320
You can set up password
policies, be it basic,

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.360
standard, or strong.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.150
You also have some additional
settings on the device

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.960
that you can control, like
you can pick if notifications

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.780
are allowed to be viewed
on the lock screen

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.460
and if you want
managed apps to be

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.800
able to sync using mobile data.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.950
Or if you want the user
to be able to back up

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.590
the device with iCloud,
some Safari settings,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.830
and some specific settings
are on photos, screen capture,

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.120
and Siri.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.000
Now, once you as an admin
have decided and applied

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.060
all the settings you want
to enforce on these devices,

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.310
you just have to turn
on device management,

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.470
send out communications
to your employees

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.530
to start enrolling
their devices.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.460
Now, let's see what the
user experience looks like.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.009
So this is my iPad.

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:12.540
I have my personal Gmail on it.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.780
To enroll a device,
you first have

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.290
to download the Google Device
Policy App from the App Store.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:26.460
And then, once it downloads,
you log in with G Suite account.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.940
This is my super
secret password.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.890
Accept the terms and conditions,
and install the profile.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.040
This is the G Suite MDM profile.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.180
It takes a bit.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.090
At this point, if you are
required admin approval,

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.780
the user won't see anything till
the admin approves this device.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.910
I've set it up for
automatic approval, though,

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.830
so it's pretty instant.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:50.120
We need to put in our password
one more time to sync email.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.440
It has synced mail,
contacts, and calendar

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.710
here in the native mailer.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.605
Now, let's go
check out our mail.

00:03:00.605 --> 00:03:02.210
There's two accounts here--

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:06.500
my personal Gmail, and
the G Suite work account.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.330
Now, let's say I
lost this device.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.230
The G Suite admin can simply
wipe my corporate email

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.150
from the console
sitting in his office,

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:17.150
and ensure that all
the work data is safe.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.070
He has the device,
we just enroll.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.290
Since this is my
personal device,

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:24.110
I'll only have the admin
wipe my work email,

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.300
and leave everything
is on there.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.820
If it's a corporate
device, we can potentially

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:30.890
wipe the whole device, too.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.510
The comment has been sent.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:34.400
Going back to the
device, you can

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.830
see that there's only
one account now--

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.180
my personal one.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:38.970
That's it.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.025
It's as simple as that.

00:03:40.025 --> 00:03:41.900
STEPHANIE WONG: Wow,
that was pretty amazing.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.730
For sure we're going to win
the throne with that one.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.355
SIRI CHERUKURI: If
only winning thrones

00:03:45.355 --> 00:03:48.380
was as easy as mobile device
management with Google Cloud.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:49.460
STEPHANIE WONG: If you want
to get in touch with us,

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.270
go ahead and click
on the link below.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.790
SIRI CHERUKURI: And if you
like what you saw today,

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.280
please like, share,
and subscribe.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:57.930
[MUSIC PLAYING]

